    "background_story": "Wayne was a linguistics professor with a passion for words and their meanings. He spent most of his career studying the intricacies of language, particularly the concept of antonymy - the relationship between words with opposite meanings. Wayne's fascination with antonymy led him to create a groundbreaking theory that challenged traditional notions of language. He proposed that antonyms were not mutually exclusive, but rather, they existed on a spectrum, with words often embodying both contradictory meanings simultaneously. Wayne's work sparked a heated debate in the academic community, with some hailing him as a genius and others dismissing his ideas as absurd. Despite the controversy, Wayne remained committed to his research, convinced that the complexities of antonymy held the key to understanding the human experience.",
